  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "NOMINAL switches between continuous x87 FYL2X/F2XM1 at n <= 2 and stored x87 pow at n >= 3, drifting 22 ULP on 4 periods",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20228 through 20527, NOMINAL(effect_rate, npery) truncates npery toward zero (returning #NUM! for effect_rate <= 0 or truncated npery < 1), computes base = RN53(RN64(1 + effect_rate)) and reciprocal = 1 / periods, uses register-continuous x87 FYL2X/F2XM1/FSCALE for periods <= 2 and the stored-LN/product/EXP chain for periods >= 3, and returns periods * (powered - 1). On =NOMINAL(0.053543,4), this produces 0.052500319868356016 (0x3faae15269ba6f00), 22 ULP above the exact mathematical value.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20228/20430 (120/120 pinned and 2,085/2,085 full-bank NOMINAL rows) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in dc96l3_x87 and prefix_metadata (row 371).",
